# Directory Structure — Node.js / Express

## Standard structure

```
src/
├── app.js (or app.ts)          ← Init Express app, register middleware and routes
├── server.js                   ← Bootstrap server, listen on port — no business logic
└── modules/
    └── <domain>/               ← One directory per domain (users, auth, products)
        ├── <domain>.router.js  ← Route declarations, calls controller
        ├── <domain>.controller.js ← Receives req/res, calls service, returns response
        ├── <domain>.service.js ← Business logic
        └── <domain>.test.js    ← Unit tests for service

middleware/
├── auth.js                     ← Authentication middleware
├── errorHandler.js             ← Global error handler
└── validate.js                 ← Input validation middleware

config/
└── index.js                    ← Centralized config from env vars
```

## Principles

- **Router** only declares routes and middleware chains
- **Controller** receives req → calls service → returns res. No business logic.
- **Service** contains all business logic. No dependency on req/res.
- **Global error handler** placed last in `app.js` — catches all errors
